**Draft for legal review.** The details in square brackets must be completed, and the whole text checked against the GDPR and the Mauritius Data Protection Act 2017 before launch.

## Who we are

West of Mauritius (westmauritius.mu and ouestmaurice.mu) is published by [COMPANY NAME], [ADDRESS]. We are responsible for the personal data described here. Contact: [CONTACT EMAIL].

## What we collect and why

**Property enquiries.** When you send the "Live in the West" form we store your name, email address, phone or WhatsApp number (if given), country, budget, timeframe, areas of interest, message, newsletter choice, language and the page you came from. With your consent, we share these details with selected property developers and estate agents on the west coast of Mauritius so that they can contact you about your enquiry. Legal basis: your consent. You can withdraw it at any time by writing to us; this does not affect sharing that already took place.

**Contact form.** We store your name, email address, subject and message in order to reply. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in answering messages.

**Newsletter.** We store your email address and language, and send a confirmation link first: nothing is sent until you confirm. Every newsletter contains an unsubscribe link. Legal basis: your consent.

**Protection against spam.** To limit automated submissions we keep a scrambled (salted hash) form of your IP address for up to 24 hours. It is not used for anything else.

**Visitor statistics.** We use Umami, which counts visits without cookies and without collecting personal data.

**Maps.** Maps are loaded from OpenFreeMap; your browser connects to their servers to fetch map images.

## Who receives your data

- Property developers and estate agents on the west coast, only for property enquiries, and only with your consent.
- Service providers who process data on our behalf: Cloudflare (hosting), Neon (database), Resend (email) and Umami (statistics). Some of them may process data outside Mauritius and the European Union; [describe the safeguards, e.g. standard contractual clauses].

We never sell or share messages sent through the contact form or newsletter addresses.

## How long we keep it

- Property enquiries: [24 months] after your last contact with us.
- Contact messages: [12 months].
- Newsletter addresses: until you unsubscribe.
- Scrambled IP addresses for spam protection: 24 hours.

## Your rights

You can ask for access to your data, correction, deletion, restriction or portability, object to its use, and withdraw your consent at any time: write to [CONTACT EMAIL]. You may also complain to the Data Protection Office of Mauritius or to the data protection authority where you live (for example the CNIL in France, the ICO in the United Kingdom or the Information Regulator in South Africa).

